{"id": "unknown-2026-10-15-007", "date": "2026-10-15", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q4", "month": 10, "week": 42, "weekday": "Thu"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["industry_general"], "sentiment": {"label": "positive", "score": 0.5, "keywords": ["improve"]}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "New image dataset aims to improve AI-based navigation of PV cleaning robots", "content": "<p>Researchers have created a dataset of 6,200 solar panel images designed to support AI-based navigation of cleaning robots. The dataset features annotated panel reference lines under clean, synthetically soiled, and laboratory contamination conditions, with the aim of helping developers assess the robustness of visual navigation algorithms.</p>\n<p>The post <a href=\"https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/10/15/new-image-dataset-aims-to-improve-ai-based-navigation-of-pv-cleaning-robots/\">New image dat", "sources": [{"name": "pv_magazine", "url": "https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/10/15/new-image-dataset-aims-to-improve-ai-based-navigation-of-pv-cleaning-robots/", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "unknown-2026-10-15-008", "date": "2026-10-15", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q4", "month": 10, "week": 42, "weekday": "Thu"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["industry_general"], "sentiment": {"label": "neutral", "score": 0.0, "keywords": []}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "Octopus Energy unveils heat pump add-on for home cooling", "content": "<p>K-based Octopus Energy has introduced Cosy Cooler, a hydronic cooling unit designed to work with its existing Cosy heat pumps. The company says the device can be installed using existing radiator pipework and will cost between GBP 500 ($670) and GBP 600 when it becomes available in 2027.</p>\n<p>The post <a href=\"https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/10/15/octopus-energy-unveils-heat-pump-add-on-for-home-cooling/\">Octopus Energy unveils heat pump add-on for home cooling</a> appeared first on <a hre", "sources": [{"name": "pv_magazine", "url": "https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/10/15/octopus-energy-unveils-heat-pump-add-on-for-home-cooling/", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "unknown-2026-10-15-009", "date": "2026-10-15", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q4", "month": 10, "week": 42, "weekday": "Thu"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["installation_demand", "industry_general"], "sentiment": {"label": "neutral", "score": 0.0, "keywords": []}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "Dutch startup offers PV mounting solution for fragile roofs", "content": "<p>Dutch startup Rable has developed a self-supporting PV mounting system for fragile roofs with slopes of up to 10 degrees, reducing anchor points by 95% compared with conventional systems. The galvanized-steel structure distributes loads of 6 kg/m² to 15 kg/m² and can reduce installation costs by €0.15 ($0.16)/W, according to the company.</p>\n<p>The post <a href=\"https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/10/15/dutch-startup-offers-pv-mounting-solution-for-fragile-roofs/\">Dutch startup offers PV mountin", "sources": [{"name": "pv_magazine", "url": "https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/10/15/dutch-startup-offers-pv-mounting-solution-for-fragile-roofs/", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "unknown-2026-10-15-010", "date": "2026-10-15", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q4", "month": 10, "week": 42, "weekday": "Thu"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["industry_general"], "sentiment": {"label": "neutral", "score": 0.0, "keywords": []}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "Solaria plans 500 MW data center project powered by 350 MW of solar in Uruguay", "content": "<p>Solaria plans to invest $5.7 billion in a data center technology park in Uruguay, including 500 MW of data center capacity and 350 MW of solar PV. The government says it is the largest foreign investment ever announced in the country.</p>\n<p>The post <a href=\"https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/10/15/solaria-plans-500-mw-data-center-project-powered-by-350-mw-of-solar-in-uruguay/\">Solaria plans 500 MW data center project powered by 350 MW of solar in Uruguay</a> appeared first on <a href=\"https:/", "sources": [{"name": "pv_magazine", "url": "https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/10/15/solaria-plans-500-mw-data-center-project-powered-by-350-mw-of-solar-in-uruguay/", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "unknown-2026-10-15-011", "date": "2026-10-15", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q4", "month": 10, "week": 42, "weekday": "Thu"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["industry_general"], "sentiment": {"label": "neutral", "score": 0.0, "keywords": []}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "Saudi Arabia uses 250 MW solar park to breed threatened gazelles", "content": "<p>Saudi Arabia’s Prince Mohammed bin Salman Royal Reserve has introduced 38 Sand gazelles into an operational solar facility following a seven-month trial. The project aims to use existing PV infrastructure as a breeding habitat for threatened wildlife, with the first births expected this winter.</p>\n<p>The post <a href=\"https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/10/15/saudi-arabia-uses-250-mw-solar-park-to-breed-threatened-gazelles/\">Saudi Arabia uses 250 MW solar park to breed threatened gazelles</a> a", "sources": [{"name": "pv_magazine", "url": "https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/10/15/saudi-arabia-uses-250-mw-solar-park-to-breed-threatened-gazelles/", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "unknown-2026-10-15-012", "date": "2026-10-15", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q4", "month": 10, "week": 42, "weekday": "Thu"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["installation_demand", "industry_general"], "sentiment": {"label": "negative", "score": -0.5, "keywords": ["slow", "weak"]}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "Germany deploys 12.76 GW of solar in first nine months of 2026", "content": "<p>Germany installed 1.23 GW of solar capacity in September, down from 1.64 GW in August, as utility-scale additions hit their lowest level of 2026 and rooftop demand remained weak. Despite the slowdown, installations in the first nine months of 2026 reached 12.76 GW, slightly above the same period last year.</p>\n<p>The post <a href=\"https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/10/15/germany-deploys-12-76-gw-of-solar-in-first-nine-months-of-2026/\">Germany deploys 12.76 GW of solar in first nine months of 20", "sources": [{"name": "pv_magazine", "url": "https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/10/15/germany-deploys-12-76-gw-of-solar-in-first-nine-months-of-2026/", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "unknown-2026-10-15-013", "date": "2026-10-15", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q4", "month": 10, "week": 42, "weekday": "Thu"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["industry_general"], "sentiment": {"label": "neutral", "score": 0.0, "keywords": []}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "India’s solar industry faces workforce readiness gap", "content": "<p>A Mercom India study has found that solar industry employers across project development, manufacturing, rooftop solar, and engineering, procurement, and construction (EPC) often need to spend months training fresh graduates before they are ready to contribute effectively.</p>\n<p>The post <a href=\"https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/10/15/indias-solar-industry-faces-workforce-readiness-gap-mercom/\">India’s solar industry faces workforce readiness gap</a> appeared first on <a href=\"https://www.pv-", "sources": [{"name": "pv_magazine", "url": "https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/10/15/indias-solar-industry-faces-workforce-readiness-gap-mercom/", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "unknown-2026-10-15-014", "date": "2026-10-15", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q4", "month": 10, "week": 42, "weekday": "Thu"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["industry_general"], "sentiment": {"label": "negative", "score": -0.5, "keywords": ["weak"]}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "Finland demands grid-forming support for new wind, solar in weak grids", "content": "<p>Fingrid will require new wind and solar plants in Finland’s weakest grid areas to provide grid-forming capability, which developers can meet with co-located batteries sized at up to 30% of plant output. </p>\n<p>The post <a href=\"https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/10/15/finland-demands-grid-forming-support-for-new-wind-solar-in-weak-grids/\">Finland demands grid-forming support for new wind, solar in weak grids</a> appeared first on <a href=\"https://www.pv-magazine.com\">pv magazine Global</a>.</p", "sources": [{"name": "pv_magazine", "url": "https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/10/15/finland-demands-grid-forming-support-for-new-wind-solar-in-weak-grids/", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "unknown-2026-10-15-015", "date": "2026-10-15", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q4", "month": 10, "week": 42, "weekday": "Thu"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["industry_general"], "sentiment": {"label": "positive", "score": 0.5, "keywords": ["expand"]}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "Mova launches residential battery with integrated EV charging management", "content": "<p>The Mova LumeGret S5000 residential energy storage system combines solar power management, expandable battery storage, and electric vehicle charging. The system supports up to 4.8 kW of solar input and can be paired with a 7 kW EV charger.</p>\n<p>The post <a href=\"https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/10/15/mova-launches-residential-battery-with-integrated-ev-charging-management/\">Mova launches residential battery with integrated EV charging management</a> appeared first on <a href=\"https://www.pv", "sources": [{"name": "pv_magazine", "url": "https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/10/15/mova-launches-residential-battery-with-integrated-ev-charging-management/", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "unknown-2026-10-15-016", "date": "2026-10-15", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q4", "month": 10, "week": 42, "weekday": "Thu"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["industry_general"], "sentiment": {"label": "positive", "score": 0.75, "keywords": ["leading", "increase"]}, "importance": {"score": 0.65, "reasons": ["情緒極端"]}, "title": "Scientists develop moth-eye-inspired antireflective surfaces for PV modules", "content": "<p>Researchers in Portugal have investigated the mechanical durability of moth-eye-inspired antireflective silicon surfaces for photovoltaic applications. They found that repeated sliding causes nanopillar fracture and material compaction, with higher mechanical loads leading to increased friction and wear.</p>\n<p>The post <a href=\"https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/10/15/scientists-develop-moth-eye-inspired-antireflective-surfaces-for-pv-modules/\">Scientists develop moth-eye-inspired antireflecti", "sources": [{"name": "pv_magazine", "url": "https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/10/15/scientists-develop-moth-eye-inspired-antireflective-surfaces-for-pv-modules/", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "unknown-2026-10-15-017", "date": "2026-10-15", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q4", "month": 10, "week": 42, "weekday": "Thu"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["industry_general"], "sentiment": {"label": "negative", "score": -0.25, "keywords": ["growth", "decline"]}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "China solar down 29%, everywhere else up 15%", "content": "BloombergNEF’s projection that solar industry would decline for the first time in decades, has proven prescient with China capacity down over 100 GW, while the world has continued a measured pace of growth.", "sources": [{"name": "pv_magazine_usa", "url": "https://pv-magazine-usa.com/2026/10/15/china-solar-down-29-everywhere-else-up-15/", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "unknown-2026-10-15-018", "date": "2026-10-15", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q4", "month": 10, "week": 42, "weekday": "Thu"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["industry_general"], "sentiment": {"label": "neutral", "score": 0.0, "keywords": []}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "RFP alert: New York State announces over $37 million for cleantech business accelerators", "content": "The newly established Commercialization Cohort Initiative seeks to launch four business accelerators to train, mentor and fund clean energy startups and entrepreneurs.", "sources": [{"name": "pv_magazine_usa", "url": "https://pv-magazine-usa.com/2026/10/15/rfp-alert-new-york-state-announces-over-37-million-for-cleantech-business-accelerators/", "type": "rss"}]}
